{"availability":"available","full":"egladman/magus","name":"magus","description":"A fast, cross-platform build system and task orchestrator for polyglot monorepos. One statically linked Go binary, no second toolchain to install.","category":"Productivity","language":"Go","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-10T00:14:02Z","updated":"2026-10-11T08:21:01Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"http://eli.gladman.cc/magus/","topics":["agentic","ai-agents","build-system","build-tool","buzz","cli","developer-tools","go","golang","knowledge-base","knowledge-graph","mcp","mcp-server","monorepo","nx","offline-first","polyglot","pwa","task-orchestration","task-runner"],"demo":"https://eli.gladman.cc/magus/console/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:52.774Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:52.774Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:52.774Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T14:52:52.774Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A fast, cross-platform task orchestrator for polyglot monorepos. One binary, no second toolchain to install. Targets are programs, not YAML.","Change a file and magus works out which projects it reaches, rebuilds only those, and caches every result so the same work never runs twice.","magus informs; it never decides. It hands you everything it knows about your repository (what a change reaches, which files are generated, where a symbol is used) and the call stays yours. It was built for humans, not for agents: agents drive it well anyway, because an interface legible to a person is legible to anything, and that ordering is the design."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/egladman/magus/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8713c8fd1e5e808447aa9caf10033af08852f874ed7679afd2261fa26da552fe","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:52.928Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T14:52:52.928Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A fast, cross-p